{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781547835182,"sessionID":"ses_13379ab6affeuO2BC4TQn53EPH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_mFT9p8fduJvRoraFgzoiigyX","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/output_contract.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/output_contract.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deliverable Contract\n2: \n3: Create an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n4: \n5: ## `answer/audit_findings.md`\n6: \n7: Audit the prior work before presenting corrected decisions.\n8: \n9: Required facts:\n10: \n11: - Which prior facts or decisions should be preserved.\n12: - Which prior facts or decisions should be corrected.\n13: - Which expense, if any, was omitted from the prior draft.\n14: - Which award cap source controls and why.\n15: - Local evidence file names supporting preservation and correction decisions.\n16: \n17: ## `answer/corrected_expense_decisions.md`\n18: \n19: Write the corrected expense decision table.\n20: \n21: Required facts:\n22: \n23: - One row or entry for every expense ID in `04_expenses.csv`.\n24: - For each expense: requested amount, approved amount, approve/reject/partial decision, and reason.\n25: - The volunteer refreshments cap when applied.\n26: - The receipt rule when applied.\n27: - The corrected reimbursable total.\n28: \n29: ## `answer/final_closeout_summary.md`\n30: \n31: Write the final closeout summary for the program manager.\n32: \n33: Required facts:\n34: \n35: - Correct award cap and source.\n36: - Correct reimbursable total.\n37: - Remaining amount under the cap.\n38: - Preserved useful prior work.\n39: - Corrected wrong prior work.\n40: - Outcome facts from the local outcome note.\n41: \n42: Rules:\n43: \n44: - Use local files only.\n45: - Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n46: - Preserve correct prior work when it is supported by the current local evidence.\n47: - Extra scratch files are allowed, but the three named deliverables under `answer/` are the review packet.\n\n(End of file - total 47 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/audit_findings.md`\n\nAudit the prior work before presenting corrected decisions.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- Which prior facts or decisions should be preserved.\n- Which prior facts or decisions should be corrected.\n- Which expense, if any, was omitted from the prior draft.\n- Which award cap source controls and why.\n- Local evidence file names supporting preservation and correction decisions.\n\n## `answer/corrected_expense_decisions.md`\n\nWrite the corrected expense decision table.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/output_contract.md","text":"# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/audit_findings.md`\n\nAudit the prior work before presenting corrected decisions.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- Which prior facts or decisions should be preserved.\n- Which prior facts or decisions should be corrected.\n- Which expense, if any, was omitted from the prior draft.\n- Which award cap source controls and why.\n- Local evidence file names supporting preservation and correction decisions.\n\n## `answer/corrected_expense_decisions.md`\n\nWrite the corrected expense decision table.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every expense ID in `04_expenses.csv`.\n- For each expense: requested amount, approved amount, approve/reject/partial decision, and reason.\n- The volunteer refreshments cap when applied.\n- The receipt rule when applied.\n- The corrected reimbursable total.\n\n## `answer/final_closeout_summary.md`\n\nWrite the final closeout summary for the program manager.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- Correct award cap and source.\n- Correct reimbursable total.\n- Remaining amount under the cap.\n- Preserved useful prior work.\n- Corrected wrong prior work.\n- Outcome facts from the local outcome note.\n\nRules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n- Preserve correct prior work when it is supported by the current local evidence.\n- Extra scratch files are allowed, but the three named deliverables under `answer/` are the review packet.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":47,"totalLines":47,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/output_contract.md","time":{"start":1781547835114,"end":1781547835165}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0ba44c6ba21229db016a30433b185c8191b9cd95ff02702ec9"}},"id":"prt_ecc869ee300178vu8HHaEBdI5r","sessionID":"ses_13379ab6affeuO2BC4TQn53EPH","messageID":"msg_ecc867a460015J4UkJWEizPEoJ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781547835182,"sessionID":"ses_13379ab6affeuO2BC4TQn53EPH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_gAM0q06oxHnSn4XY03IbR4D7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/00_closeout_request.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/00_closeout_request.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Closeout Request\n2: \n3: Request date: 2026-05-24\n4: \n5: The neighborhood garden mini-grant needs a corrected closeout packet for finance review.\n6: \n7: The prior analyst already drafted expense decisions and a short summary in `prior_work/`. Some of that work is useful, but some of it used stale award information or missed current reimbursement rules.\n8: \n9: Use the newest dated award document when award-cap sources conflict. Preserve correct decisions and outcome facts instead of rewriting the packet from scratch.\n\n(End of file - total 9 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Closeout Request\n\nRequest date: 2026-05-24\n\nThe neighborhood garden mini-grant needs a corrected closeout packet for finance review.\n\nThe prior analyst already drafted expense decisions and a short summary in `prior_work/`. Some of that work is useful, but some of it used stale award information or missed current reimbursement rules.\n\nUse the newest dated award document when award-cap sources conflict. Preserve correct decisions and outcome facts instead of rewriting the packet from scratch.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/00_closeout_request.md","text":"# Closeout Request\n\nRequest date: 2026-05-24\n\nThe neighborhood garden mini-grant needs a corrected closeout packet for finance review.\n\nThe prior analyst already drafted expense decisions and a short summary in `prior_work/`. Some of that work is use