k/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n+| `G-005` approved at `$310.00` | Change to rejection at `$0.00` | Public outreach printing is not listed as an eligible category in the current rules, and the expense is over `$75.00` without a receipt, so it also fails the receipt rule. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n+| Draft reimbursable total of `$1,855.00` | Replace with `$1,588.00` | The corrected total reflects the `G-002` partial cap, the `G-005` rejection, and the omitted `G-006` approval. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n+| Draft remaining amount under cap of `$145.00` | Replace with `$12.00` | The remaining amount must be calculated against the corrected `$1,600.00` cap and corrected `$1,588.00` reimbursable total. | `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`, `prior_work/draft_closeout_summary.md` |\n+\n+## Omitted Expense\n+\n+The prior draft omitted `G-006` (`Final report postage`). It should be approved for `$68.00` because public outreach postage is eligible, the amount is `$75.00` or less, and the ledger includes a note, so a receipt is not required.\n+\n+Evidence files: `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_closeout_summary.md`\n+\n+## Controlling Award Cap Source\n+\n+The controlling award cap source is `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`, which sets the final reimbursement cap at `$1,600.00` and explicitly supersedes the original award letter. It controls because the closeout request and allowability rules both instruct reviewers to use the newest dated award document when award-cap sources conflict.\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/corrected_expense_decisions.md\n+# Corrected Expense Decisions\n+\n+| Expense ID | Requested amount | Approved amount | Decision | Reason |\n+| --- | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n+| G-001 | 980.00 | 980.00 | approve | Garden supplies are eligible, and a receipt is on file. |\n+| G-002 | 145.00 | 120.00 | partial | Volunteer refreshments are eligible only up to the `$120.00` event cap. |\n+| G-003 | 420.00 | 420.00 | approve | Accessibility printing is eligible, and a receipt is on file. |\n+| G-004 | 160.00 | 0.00 | reject | Staff gifts are not eligible. |\n+| G-005 | 310.00 | 0.00 | reject | Public outreach printing is not listed as an eligible category, and any single expense over `$75.00` requires a receipt; this expense has no receipt on file. |\n+| G-006 | 68.00 | 68.00 | approve | Public outreach postage is eligible. Because the expense is `$75.00` or less and the ledger includes a note, it may be approved without a receipt. |\n+\n+## Corrected Reimbursable Total\n+\n+`$1,588.00`\n+\n+## Rules Applied\n+\n+- Volunteer refreshments cap applied to `G-002`: maximum allowable reimbursement is `$120.00`.\n+- Receipt rule applied to `G-005`: over `$75.00` without a receipt, so it cannot be approved.\n+- Receipt rule applied to `G-006`: `$75.00` or less with a ledger note, so it can be approved without a receipt.\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md\n+# Final Closeout Summary\n+\n+The correct reimbursement cap is `$1,600.00`, based on `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`. That award update is the newest dated award document and explicitly supersedes the original `02_award_letter_2026-04-15.md`, so it controls for closeout.\n+\n+The corrected reimbursable total is `$1,588.00`, leaving `$12.00` remaining under the cap.\n+\n+Useful prior work was preserved where supported by the local evidence:\n+\n+- `G-001` remained fully approved at `$980.00`.\n+- `G-003` remained fully approved at `$420.00`.\n+- `G-004` remained rejected because staff gifts are not eligible.\n+- The prior outcome facts about 140 seedling starter kits and 36 Braille outreach flyers were retained.\n+\n+Wrong prior work was corrected where the local evidence required changes:\n+\n+- The draft cap of `$2,000.00` was replaced with the correct `$1,600.00` cap from the newer award update.\n+- `G-002` was reduced from `$145.00` to `$120.00` because volunteer refreshments are capped at `$120.00`.\n+- `G-005` was changed from approved to rejected because public outreach printing is not listed as eligible in the current rules and the expense is over `$75.00` without a receipt.\n+- The omitted `G-006` postage expense was added and approved at `$68.00` because public outreach postage is eligible and the amount is within the no-receipt threshold with a ledger note.\n+\n+Outcome facts from `05_outcomes.md`:\n+\n+- 140 seedling starter kits were distributed.\n+- 36 Braille outreach flyers were printed for accessible pickup locations.\n+- 18 volunteer setup shifts were completed.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/audit_findings.md\nA tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/corrected_expense_decisions.md\nA tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/audit_findings.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/audit_findings.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/audit_findings.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@\n+# Audit Findings\n+\n+## Preserve From Prior Work\n+\n+| Prior item | Preserve? | Why | Evidence files |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| `G-001` approved at `$980.00` | Yes | Garden supplies are eligible, receipt is on file, and the full amount is allowable. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n+| `G-003` approved at `$420.00` | Yes | Accessibility printing is eligible, receipt is on file, and the full amount is allowable. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work