{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781547913995,"sessionID":"ses_13379ab6affeuO2BC4TQn53EPH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_4nUQAGhILd4oOC7sNayaw69x","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md","offset":1,"limit":300},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Final Closeout Summary\n2: \n3: The correct reimbursement cap is `$1,600.00`, based on `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`. That award update is the newest dated award document and explicitly supersedes the original `02_award_letter_2026-04-15.md`, so it controls for closeout.\n4: \n5: The corrected reimbursable total is `$1,588.00`, leaving `$12.00` remaining under the cap.\n6: \n7: Useful prior work was preserved where supported by the local evidence:\n8: \n9: - `G-001` remained fully approved at `$980.00`.\n10: - `G-003` remained fully approved at `$420.00`.\n11: - `G-004` remained rejected because staff gifts are not eligible.\n12: - The prior outcome facts about 140 seedling starter kits and 36 Braille outreach flyers were retained.\n13: \n14: Wrong prior work was corrected where the local evidence required changes:\n15: \n16: - The draft cap of `$2,000.00` was replaced with the correct `$1,600.00` cap from the newer award update.\n17: - `G-002` was reduced from `$145.00` to `$120.00` because volunteer refreshments are capped at `$120.00`.\n18: - `G-005` was changed from approved to rejected because public outreach printing is not listed as eligible in the current rules and the expense is over `$75.00` without a receipt.\n19: - The omitted `G-006` postage expense was added and approved at `$68.00` because public outreach postage is eligible and the amount is within the no-receipt threshold with a ledger note.\n20: \n21: Outcome facts from `05_outcomes.md`:\n22: \n23: - 140 seedling starter kits were distributed.\n24: - 36 Braille outreach flyers were printed for accessible pickup locations.\n25: - 18 volunteer setup shifts were completed.\n\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Final Closeout Summary\n\nThe correct reimbursement cap is `$1,600.00`, based on `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`. That award update is the newest dated award document and explicitly supersedes the original `02_award_letter_2026-04-15.md`, so it controls for closeout.\n\nThe corrected reimbursable total is `$1,588.00`, leaving `$12.00` remaining under the cap.\n\nUseful prior work was preserved where supported by the local evidence:\n\n- `G-001` remained fully approved at `$980.00`.\n- `G-003` remained fully approved at `$420.00`.\n- `G-004` remained rejected because staff gifts are not eligible.\n- The prior outcome facts about 140 seedling starter kits and 36 Braille outreach flyers were retained.\n\nWrong prior work was corrected where the local evidence required changes:\n\n- The draft cap of `$2,000.00` was replaced with the correct `$1,600.00` cap from the newer award update.\n- `G-002` was reduced from `$145.00` to `$120.00` because volunteer refreshments are capped at `$120.00`.\n- `G-005` was changed from approved to rejected because public outreach printing is not listed as eligible in the current rules and the expense is over `$75.00` without a receipt.\n- The omitted `G-006` postage expense was added and approved at `$68.00` because public outreach postage is eligible and the amount is within the no-receipt threshold with a ledger note.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md","text":"# Final Closeout Summary\n\nThe correct reimbursement cap is `$1,600.00`, based on `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`. That award update is the newest dated award document and explicitly supersedes the original `02_award_letter_2026-04-15.md`, so it controls for closeout.\n\nThe corrected reimbursable total is `$1,588.00`, leaving `$12.00` remaining under the cap.\n\nUseful prior work was preserved where supported by the local evidence:\n\n- `G-001` remained fully approved at `$980.00`.\n- `G-003` remained fully approved at `$420.00`.\n- `G-004` remained rejected because staff gifts are not eligible.\n- The prior outcome facts about 140 seedling starter kits and 36 Braille outreach flyers were retained.\n\nWrong prior work was corrected where the local evidence required changes:\n\n- The draft cap of `$2,000.00` was replaced with the correct `$1,600.00` cap from the newer award update.\n- `G-002` was reduced from `$145.00` to `$120.00` because volunteer refreshments are capped at `$120.00`.\n- `G-005` was changed from approved to rejected because public outreach printing is not listed as eligible in the current rules and the expense is over `$75.00` without a receipt.\n- The omitted `G-006` postage expense was added and approved at `$68.00` because public outreach postage is eligible and the amount is within the no-receipt threshold with a ledger note.\n\nOutcome facts from `05_outcomes.md`:\n\n- 140 seedling starter kits were distributed.\n- 36 Braille outreach flyers were printed for accessible pickup locations.\n- 18 volunteer setup shifts were completed.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":25,"totalLines":25,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md","time":{"start":1781547913965,"end":1781547913989}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_05a5095692964030016a304389e9c08191b0dfd211c8f4fdfe"}},"id":"prt_ecc87d2e3001KyQFLv1qMNgOlM","sessionID":"ses_13379ab6affeuO2BC4TQn53EPH","messageID":"msg_ecc87be1f001vhrNdJIH8Lhthi"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781547913995,"sessionID":"ses_13379ab6affeuO2BC4TQn53EPH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_hwl0fgE73DiTGrG3YfiWRqg4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/audit_findings.md","offset":1,"limit":300},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/audit_findings.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Audit Findings\n2: \n3: ## Preserve From Prior Work\n4: \n5: | Prior item | Preserve? | Why | Evidence files |\n6: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n7: | `G-001` approved at `$980.00` | Yes | Garden supplies are eligible, receipt is on file, and the full amount is allowable. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n8: | `G-003` approved at `$420.00` | Yes | Accessibility printing is eligible, receipt is on file, and the full amount is allowable. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n9: | `G-004` rejected at `$0.00` | Yes | Staff gifts are not eligible. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n10: | Outcome facts on seedling kits and Braille flyers | Yes | Both outcome statements match the local outcomes note. | `05_outcomes.md`, `prior_work/draft_closeout_summary.md` |\n11: \n12: ## Correct Prior Work\n13: \n14: | Prior item | Correction | Why | Evidence files |\n15: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n16: | Draft award cap of `$2,000.00` | Replace with `$1,600.00` | The closeout request and allowability rules say to use the newest dated award document when award sources conflict. The `2026-05-22` award update supersedes the `2026-04-15` original letter. | `00_closeout_request.md`, `01_allowability_rules.md`, `02_award_letter_2026-04-15.md`, `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`, `prior_work/draft_closeout_summary.md` |\n17: | `G-002` approved at `$145.00` | Change to partial approval of `$120.00` | Volunteer refreshments are eligible only up to `$120.00` for this event. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n18: | `G-005` approved at `$310.00` | Change to rejection at `$0.00` | Public outreach printing is not listed as an eligible category in the current rules, and the expense is over `$75.00` without a receipt, so it also fails the receipt rule. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n19: | Draft reimbursable total of `$1,855.00` | Replace with `$1,588.00` | The corrected total reflects the `G-002` partial cap, the `G-005` rejection, and the omitted `G-006` approval. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n20: | Draft remaining amount under cap of `$145.00` | Replace with `$12.00` | The remaining amount must be calculated against the corrected `$1,600.00` cap and corrected `$1,588.00` reimbursable total. | `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`, `prior_work/draft_closeout_summary.md` |\n21: \n22: ## Omitted Expense\n23: \n24: The prior draft omitted `G-006` (`Final report postage`). It should be approved for `$68.00` because public outreach postage is eligible, the amount is `$75.00` or less, and the ledger includes a note, so a receipt is not required.\n25: \n26: Evidence files: `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_closeout_summary.md`\n27: \n28: ## Controlling Award Cap Source\n29: \n30: The controlling award cap source is `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`, which sets the final reimbursement cap at `$1,600.00` and explicitly supersedes the original award letter. It controls because the closeout request and allowability rules both instruct reviewers to use the newest dated award document when award-cap sources conflict.\n\n(End of file - total 30 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Audit Findings\n\n## Preserve From Prior Work\n\n| Prior item | Preserve? | Why | Evidence files |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `G-001` approved at `$980.00` | Yes | Garden supplies are eligible, receipt is on file, and the full amount is allowable. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n| `G-003` approved at `$420.00` | Yes | Accessibility printing is eligible, receipt is on file, and the full amount is allowable. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n| `G-004` rejected at `$0.00` | Yes | Staff gifts are not eligible. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n| Outcome facts on seedling kits and Braille flyers | Yes | Both outcome statements match the local outcomes note. | `05_outcomes.md`, `prior_work/draft_closeout_summary.md` |\n\n## Correct Prior Work\n\n| Prior item | Correction | Why | Evidence files |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Draft award cap of `$2,000.00` | Replace with `$1,600.00` | The closeout request and allowability rules say to use the newest dated award document when award sources conflict. The `2026-05-22` award update supersedes the `2026-04-15` original letter. | `00_closeout_request.md`, `01_allowability_rules.md`, `02_award_letter_2026-04-15.md`, `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`, `prior_work/draft_closeout_summary.md` |\n| `G-002` approved at `$145.00` | Change to partial approval of `$120.00` | Volunteer refreshments are eligible only up to `$120.00` for this event. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n| `G-005` approved at `$310.00` | Change to rejection at `$0.00` | Public outreach printing is not listed as an eligible category in the current rules, and the expense is over `$75.00` without a receipt, so it also fails the receipt rule. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n| Draft reimbursable total of `$1,855.00` | Replace with `$1,588.00` | The corrected total reflects the `G-002` partial cap, the `G-005` rejection, and the omitted `G-006` approval. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n| Draft remaining amount under cap of `$145.00` | Replace with `$12.00` | The remaining amount must be calculated against the corrected `$1,600.00` cap and corrected `$1,588.00` reimbursable total. | `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`, `prior_work/draft_closeout_summary.md` |","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/audit_findings.md","text":"# Audit Findings\n\n## Preserve From Prior Work\n\n| Prior item | Preserve? | Why | Evidence files |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `G-001` approved at `$980.00` | Yes | Garden supplies are eligible, receipt is on file, and the full amount is allowable. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n| `G-003` approved at `$420.00` | Yes | Accessibility printing is eligible, receipt is on file, and the full amount is allowable. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n| `G-004` rejected at `$0.00` | Yes | Staff gifts are not eligible. | `01_allowability_rules.md`, `04_expenses.csv`, `prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md` |\n| Outcome facts on seedling kits and Braille flyers | Yes | Both outcome statements match the local outcomes note. | `05_outcomes.md`, `prior_work/draft_closeout_summary.md` |\n\n## Correct Prior Work\n\n| Prior item | Correction | Why | Evidence files |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Draft award cap of `$2,000.00` | Replace with `$1,600.00` | The closeout request and allowability rules say to use the newest dated award document when award sources conflict. The `2026-05-22` award update supersedes the `2026-04-15` original letter. | `00_closeout_request.md`, `01_allowability_rules.md`, `02_award_letter_2026-04-15.md